# customer-template-pricing

Full guidance: `.cursor/skills/rlm-customer-demo-pricing/SKILL.md`.
Lessons 1-8: `datasets/sfdmu/customer-template/en-US/customer-template-pricing/README.md`.

## Two-phase load

| Phase | Task | Mechanism | Objects |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `insert_customer_demo_pricing_data` | SFDMU | `AttributeBasedAdjRule` Upsert |
| 2 | `insert_customer_demo_pricing_adjustments` | Apex | AAC + ABA Insert |

## AAC/ABA cannot use SFDMU

For `Insert`, SFDMU resolves FK columns from the parent's SOURCE collection. `Readonly`
parents live in TARGET only, so SOURCE is empty and every child row is silently filtered
(`SOURCE: 0`). Restructuring `objectSets` or splitting into separate SFDMU tasks does not
fix it. Use the Apex task. The CSVs remain as shape documentation.

## Apex constraints

- `Operator` is the word `equals`, never `=` (`INVALID_OR_NULL_FOR_RESTRICTED_PICKLIST`).
- Omit ABA read-only fields from constructors: `AttributeAdjConditionsHash`,
  `AttributeCount`, `PricingTerm`, `PricingTermUnit`, `ScheduleType`, `SellingModelType`.
  Including any is a compile error. Leave them blank in CSVs.
- `AttributeAdjustmentCondition` has no direct delete DML — it is master-detail. Delete
  `AttributeBasedAdjustment` first, then `AttributeBasedAdjRule` (cascades AAC).
- Scope deletes to the customer prefix. Never use `DeleteSFDMUData` here — it would wipe
  coexisting QB pricing data.

## export.json

SELECT must use direct ID fields (`AttributeBasedAdjRuleId`, `AttributeDefinitionId`,
`ProductId`), not traversals. Traversal fields trigger "Referenced field removed" and a
`COMMAND_UNEXPECTED_ERROR` crash during INSERT payload construction.

## AAC CSV shape

11 columns; five value columns are empty for string conditions, requiring six commas between
`AttributeDefinition.Code` and `Operator`. One missing comma shifts `equals` into
`IntegerValue` and SFDMU reads zero source records.

`RULE;ATTR;SKU,RULE,ATTR,,,,,,equals,SKU,Enterprise`

## Verification

ABA count per SKU must equal `ExpectedPricingRules` in
`scripts/customer-demo/customer-pricebook-entries.csv`.
